{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4556","published":"2026-10-29T09:02:53Z","modified":"2026-10-29T09:15:29.222545734Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-107651"],"summary":"eog security update","details":"EOG is an application used for viewing and cataloging image files on the GNOME Desktop.It has basic editing capabilites.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in Eye of GNOME (eog). A heap-based buffer overflow exists in the PNG metadata reader due to improper state handling when parsing split metadata chunks. A remote attacker could exploit this flaw by enticing a user into opening a specially crafted PNG file, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution or a Denial of Service (DoS) via application crash.(CVE-2026-107651)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"eog","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/eog&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["eog-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","eog-debuginfo-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","eog-debugsource-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","eog-devel-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","eog-tests-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["eog-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["eog-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","eog-debuginfo-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","eog-debugsource-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","eog-devel-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","eog-tests-3.38.3-5.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-4556.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.openeuler.org/zh/security/security-bulletins/detail/?id=openEuler-SA-2026-4556"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-107651"}],"database_specific":{"severity":"Medium"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"}]}